---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
import Header from '@/components/layout/Header.astro'
import Main from '@/components/layout/Main.astro'
import Footer from '@/components/layout/Footer.astro'
import PageHeader from '@/components/ui/PageHeader.astro'
import NewTabIndicator from '@/components/ui/NewTabIndicator.astro'
import { staticPageMeta } from '@/data/static-pages'
import { PROSE_CONTENT_CLASSES } from '@/utils/prose'
---

<BaseLayout
    {...staticPageMeta('privacy')}
    description="What personal data philipp.fyi collects, why it's processed, and what rights you have under the GDPR."
    robots="noindex"
>
    <Header />
    <Main>
        <PageHeader eyebrow="Your data, explained" title="Privacy Policy">
            philipp.fyi collects a small amount of personal data through its
            contact form, hosting infrastructure, performance monitoring,
            server-side analytics, and browser security reports. This page
            explains what's collected, who processes it, and how to exercise
            your rights.
        </PageHeader>

        <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 pb-32">
            <article class={PROSE_CONTENT_CLASSES}>
                <h2>Controller</h2>
                <p>
                    Philipp Storl, based in the Chemnitz / Leipzig area,
                    Germany, is the controller responsible for the personal data
                    processed on this site (philipp.fyi). You can reach me
                    through the <a href="/contact/">contact form</a>.
                </p>

                <h2>What this site collects</h2>

                <h3>Contact form</h3>
                <p>
                    When you submit the contact form, I collect your name, email
                    address, and the message you write. Netlify Forms also
                    records your IP address, your browser's user agent, the page
                    you sent the form from (referrer), and the time of
                    submission with every message. I use this data only to
                    respond to your inquiry, after Netlify has screened it for
                    spam (see below).
                </p>
                <p>
                    Using the form is voluntary, and no law or contract requires
                    you to provide this data. The form can't be sent without all
                    three fields, though, and without your email address I can't
                    reply to you.
                </p>
                <ul>
                    <li>
                        Legal basis: Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR, my legitimate interest
                        in answering messages sent to me. Where your inquiry is
                        about working together, also Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR, steps
                        taken at your request before entering into a contract.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        Recipient:
                        <a
                            href="https://www.netlify.com/privacy/"
                            target="_blank"
                            rel="noopener noreferrer"
                            >Netlify, Inc.<NewTabIndicator
                        /></a
                        >, which stores form submissions on my behalf as a
                        processor (Netlify Forms). Netlify checks every
                        submission for spam with Akismet, a service of
                        Automattic Inc.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        Retention: kept for as long as needed to respond to and
                        follow up on your inquiry, then deleted, unless
                        statutory retention periods require keeping it longer
                        (for example, when an inquiry leads to a contract,
                        business correspondence is kept for up to 6 years under
                        §&nbsp;257 HGB and §&nbsp;147 AO). You can ask me to
                        delete it sooner at any time.
                    </li>
                </ul>

                <h3>Hosting and server logs</h3>
                <p>
                    This site is hosted on Netlify. Like most hosting providers,
                    Netlify's infrastructure automatically logs technical
                    request data (for example IP address, requested URL,
                    timestamp, and user agent) to operate, secure, and
                    troubleshoot the site.
                </p>
                <ul>
                    <li>
                        Legal basis: Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR, my legitimate interest
                        in operating a secure, reliable website.
                    </li>
                    <li>Recipient: Netlify, Inc.</li>
                    <li>
                        Retention: Netlify doesn't publish a fixed period for
                        these logs. Under
                        <a
                            href="https://www.netlify.com/privacy/"
                            target="_blank"
                            rel="noopener noreferrer"
                            >its privacy policy<NewTabIndicator
                        /></a
                        >, it keeps personal data only as long as needed for the
                        purpose it was collected for, or as long as the law
                        requires, weighing how sensitive the data is and the
                        risk of misuse.
                    </li>
                </ul>

                <h3>Performance monitoring</h3>
                <p>
                    Netlify's Real User Monitoring measures how fast pages load
                    for real visitors. On every page view, a script served from
                    this domain reads your browser's user agent, platform and
                    screen size, reduces the user agent to browser, operating
                    system and device type, and sends one record per page view
                    to Netlify: those values, the page's address, the time, and
                    load-time measurements (Core Web Vitals). Your IP address
                    reaches Netlify with that request. The script sets no
                    cookies and stores nothing in your browser. I only see
                    figures Netlify aggregates from these records.
                </p>
                <ul>
                    <li>
                        Legal basis: Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR, my legitimate interest
                        in noticing and fixing slow or broken pages.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        Reading information from your device: under §&nbsp;25(2)
                        Nr.&nbsp;2 TDDDG this needs no consent, because reading
                        these properties is strictly necessary to deliver the
                        service you requested, a website that loads and works
                        without errors. The German data protection authorities'
                        guidance on digital services (DSK Orientierungshilfe
                        Digitale Dienste, Rn. 90) counts error-free delivery of
                        a website as part of what a visitor asks for.
                    </li>
                    <li>Recipient: Netlify, Inc.</li>
                    <li>
                        Retention: on this site's Netlify plan, the figures I
                        can see cover the last 7 days, per
                        <a
                            href="https://docs.netlify.com/manage/monitoring/real-user-monitoring/"
                            target="_blank"
                            rel="noopener noreferrer"
                            >Netlify's Real User Monitoring
                            documentation<NewTabIndicator
                        /></a
                        >. Netlify doesn't publish a separate period for the
                        underlying records, so the same criteria as for the
                        hosting logs above apply.
                    </li>
                </ul>

                <h3>Site analytics</h3>
                <p>
                    To understand which pages are read and where visitors come
                    from, this site uses Netlify Analytics. It works entirely on
                    Netlify's side, from the same request logs described above:
                    no script runs in your browser and no cookies are set. It
                    processes request data such as your IP address (used to
                    count unique visitors), the page you requested, and the site
                    that referred you. I only see aggregate figures such as
                    pageviews, top pages, and referring sites, never individual
                    visitors.
                </p>
                <ul>
                    <li>
                        Legal basis: Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR, my legitimate interest
                        in understanding how the site is used.
                    </li>
                    <li>Recipient: Netlify, Inc.</li>
                    <li>
                        Retention: the figures I can see cover the last 30 days.
                        The underlying request data is the hosting logs above,
                        with the same retention.
                    </li>
                </ul>

                <h3>CSP violation reports</h3>
                <p>
                    This site's browser security policy asks your browser to
                    report any blocked or unexpected script/style activity. If
                    your browser sends one, it's stored (via Netlify Blobs) so
                    it can be investigated, then automatically deleted about 30
                    days later. A report contains the page's URL, the blocked
                    address, the referring page, the policy rule and the file
                    and line that triggered it, a short sample of the blocked
                    code, the time it was received, and your browser's user
                    agent.
                </p>
                <ul>
                    <li>
                        Legal basis: Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR, my legitimate interest
                        in detecting and fixing security issues.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        Recipients: Netlify, Inc. If a Slack alert channel is
                        configured, the report (shortened if very long),
                        including your browser's user agent, is also posted to
                        Slack (Slack Technologies Limited, Dublin, Ireland) so I
                        can investigate promptly.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        Retention: the stored copy is deleted automatically, as
                        described above. The Slack copy is kept only as long as
                        needed to investigate the violation, then deleted.
                    </li>
                </ul>

                <h2>International data transfers</h2>
                <p>
                    Netlify, Inc. is based in the United States. Where data is
                    transferred outside the European Economic Area, Netlify
                    relies on the Standard Contractual Clauses and/or the
                    EU-U.S. Data Privacy Framework as a safeguard. See
                    <a
                        href="https://www.netlify.com/privacy/"
                        target="_blank"
                        rel="noopener noreferrer"
                        >Netlify's privacy policy<NewTabIndicator
                    /></a>
                    for details. Akismet, the spam filter Netlify runs on
                    contact form submissions, is operated by Automattic Inc.,
                    also based in the United States. Netlify engages Akismet as
                    a sub-processor, and Automattic relies on the Standard
                    Contractual Clauses for transfers from the European Economic
                    Area; see
                    <a
                        href="https://automattic.com/privacy/"
                        target="_blank"
                        rel="noopener noreferrer"
                        >Automattic's privacy policy<NewTabIndicator
                    /></a
                    >.
                </p>
                <p>
                    Slack Technologies Limited, which receives CSP violation
                    reports, also processes data in the United States. For those
                    transfers Slack relies on the EU-U.S. Data Privacy Framework
                    (through its parent company Salesforce) and the Standard
                    Contractual Clauses; see
                    <a
                        href="https://slack.com/trust/privacy/privacy-policy"
                        target="_blank"
                        rel="noopener noreferrer"
                        >Slack's privacy policy<NewTabIndicator
                    /></a
                    >.
                </p>

                <h2>Cookies and local storage</h2>
                <p>
                    This site doesn't use cookies and doesn't run any
                    third-party advertising or tracking scripts. The
                    performance-monitoring script and site analytics described
                    above use no cookies or browser storage. Separately, this
                    site stores exactly one preference, your light/dark theme
                    choice, in your browser's local storage. That value never
                    leaves your browser and isn't linked to you personally.
                </p>

                <h2>Your rights</h2>
                <p>Under the GDPR, you have the right to:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li>access the personal data I hold about you (Art. 15)</li>
                    <li>have inaccurate data corrected (Art. 16)</li>
                    <li>have your data deleted (Art. 17)</li>
                    <li>restrict how your data is processed (Art. 18)</li>
                    <li>
                        receive the data you gave me in a portable format, where
                        I process it to prepare working together (Art. 20)
                    </li>
                </ul>
                <p>
                    <strong>Right to object (Art. 21):</strong> where I process
                    your data based on my legitimate interest (Art. 6(1)(f)
                    GDPR), you can object at any time, on grounds relating to
                    your particular situation. I'll then stop processing it
                    unless I can show compelling legitimate grounds that
                    override your interests, or need it to establish, exercise,
                    or defend legal claims.
                </p>
                <p>
                    To exercise any of these, use the
                    <a href="/contact/">contact form</a>. You also have the
                    right to lodge a complaint with a supervisory authority, in
                    particular the
                    <a
                        href="https://www.datenschutz.sachsen.de/"
                        target="_blank"
                        rel="noopener noreferrer"
                        >Sächsische Datenschutz- und
                        Transparenzbeauftragte<NewTabIndicator
                    /></a>
                    (the data protection authority for Saxony, Germany, where
                    I'm based), or the authority in your own country of
                    residence.
                </p>

                <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
                <p>
                    I'll update this page if what this site collects or how it's
                    processed changes. Last updated: September 25, 2026.
                </p>
            </article>
        </div>
    </Main>
    <Footer />
</BaseLayout>
